.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PBE_CIPHERINIT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PBE_CipherInit ,
.Nm EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex ,
.Nm EVP_PBE_find ,
.Nm EVP_PBE_find_ex ,
.Nm EVP_PBE_alg_add_type ,
.Nm EVP_PBE_alg_add
.Nd Password based encryption routines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_CipherInit
.Fa "ASN1_OBJECT *pbe_obj"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fa "ASN1_TYPE *param"
.Fa "EVP_CIPHER_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int en_de"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
.Fa "ASN1_OBJECT *pbe_obj"
.Fa "const char *pass"
.Fa "int passlen"
.Fa "ASN1_TYPE *param"
.Fa "EVP_CIPHER_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int en_de"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_find
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "int pbe_nid"
.Fa "int *pcnid"
.Fa "int *pmnid"
.Fa "EVP_PBE_KEYGEN **pkeygen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_find_ex
.Fa "int type"
.Fa "int pbe_nid"
.Fa "int *pcnid"
.Fa "int *pmnid"
.Fa "EVP_PBE_KEYGEN **pkeygen"
.Fa "EVP_PBE_KEYGEN_EX **keygen_ex"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_alg_add_type
.Fa "int pbe_type"
.Fa "int pbe_nid"
.Fa "int cipher_nid"
.Fa "int md_nid"
.Fa "EVP_PBE_KEYGEN *keygen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PBE_alg_add
.Fa "int nid"
.Fa "const EVP_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fa "const EVP_MD *md"
.Fa "EVP_PBE_KEYGEN *keygen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss PBE operations
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
initialise an
.Vt EVP_CIPHER_CTX
.Fa ctx
for encryption
.Pf ( Fa en_de Ns =1)
or decryption
.Pf ( Fa en_de Ns =0)
using the password
.Fa pass
of length
.Fa passlen .
The PBE algorithm type and parameters are extracted from an OID
.Fa pbe_obj
and parameters
.Fa param .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
also allows the application to specify a library context
.Fa libctx
and property query
.Fa propq
to select appropriate algorithm implementations.
.Ss PBE algorithm search
.Fn EVP_PBE_find
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_find_ex
search for a matching algorithm using two parameters:
.Pp
1. An algorithm type
.Fa type
which can be:
.Bl -bullet
.It
EVP_PBE_TYPE_OUTER - A PBE algorithm
.It
EVP_PBE_TYPE_PRF - A pseudo-random function
.It
EVP_PBE_TYPE_KDF - A key derivation function
.El
.Pp
2. A
.Fa pbe_nid
which can represent the algorithm identifier with parameters e.g.
.Sy NID_pbeWithSHA1AndRC2_CBC
or an algorithm class e.g.
.Sy NID_pbes2 .
.Pp
They return the algorithm's cipher ID
.Fa pcnid ,
digest ID
.Fa pmnid
and a key generation function for the algorithm
.Fa pkeygen .
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
also returns an extended key generation function
.Fa keygen_ex
which takes a library context and property query.
.Pp
If a NULL is supplied for any of
.Fa pcnid ,
.Fa pmnid ,
.Fa pkeygen
or
.Em pkeygen_ex
then this parameter is not returned.
.Ss PBE algorithm add
.Fn EVP_PBE_alg_add_type
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_alg_add
add an algorithm to the list of known algorithms.
Their parameters have the same meaning as for
.Fn EVP_PBE_find
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_find_ex
functions.
.Sh NOTES
The arguments
.Fa pbe_obj
and
.Fa param
to
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
together form an
.Sy X509_ALGOR
and can often be extracted directly from this structure.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Return value is 1 for success and 0 if an error occurred.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr PKCS5_PBE_keyivgen 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_PBE_keyivgen_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS5_v2_PBE_keyivgen_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_pbe_crypt_ex 3 ,
.Xr PKCS12_create_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn EVP_PBE_CipherInit_ex
and
.Fn EVP_PBE_find_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
